-    <p>The following information will provide you with an easy to navigate overview of what will happen with your personal data when you visit our website. The term “personal data” comprises all data that can be used to personally identify you. For detailed information about the subject matter of data protection, please consult our Data Protection Declaration, which we have included beneath this copy.</p>
-    
-    <h2>2. General information and mandatory information</h2>
-    <p><strong>Data protection</strong></p>
-    <p>The operators of this website and its pages take the protection of your personal data very seriously. Hence, we handle your personal data as confidential information and in compliance with the statutory data protection regulations and this Data Protection Declaration.</p>
-    <p>Whenever you use this website, a variety of personal information will be collected. Personal data comprises data that can be used to personally identify you. This Data Protection Declaration explains which data we collect as well as the purposes we use this data for. It also explains how, and for which purpose the information is collected.</p>
-    
-    <h2>3. Recording of data on our website</h2>
-    <p><strong>Cookies</strong></p>
-    <p>In some instances, our website and its pages use so-called cookies. Cookies do not cause any damage to your computer and do not contain viruses. The purpose of cookies is to make our website more user friendly, effective and more secure. Cookies are small text files that are placed on your computer and stored by your browser.</p>
+    <p>The DevTools Times is a demonstration news site. Use a unique demo password and avoid submitting sensitive personal information.</p>
+
+    <h2 id="privacy-defaults">Privacy defaults</h2>
+    <p>The shared page layout does not load third-party analytics, advertising scripts, or remote fonts. There is no optional tracking to enable or disable in this version.</p>
+    <p>Pages use a no-referrer policy to avoid sending the page address when requesting resources or following links. Some articles include externally hosted images; those hosts receive network information such as your IP address when your browser requests an image.</p>
+
+    <h2>Account forms</h2>
+    <p>Signing in and signing up require only a username and password. You can choose a username that does not identify you; we do not ask for your name, email address, phone number, or date of birth.</p>
+    <p>Only when you submit a form, your username and password are sent over HTTPS to the external authentication service at <code>us-central1-web-devrel-apps.cloudfunctions.net</code>, using its <code>/times_cdn/api/login</code> or <code>/times_cdn/api/register</code> endpoint. That service also receives network information such as your IP address. The requests omit cookies and the page referrer and do not use the browser HTTP cache.</p>
+    <p>The forms do not save credentials or returned authentication tokens in cookies, local storage, or session storage. The password field is cleared after each completed submission attempt. Your browser or password manager may separately offer to save credentials under your own settings.</p>
+    <p>This repository does not contain the authentication service. Its account retention, password storage, logging, and deletion practices cannot be verified here. Do not use a password you use elsewhere. This demo reports the authentication result but does not establish a persistent signed-in session.</p>
+
+    <h2>Reading lists and hosting</h2>
+    <p>Saving an article uses server-side session storage for its article identifier when sessions are available. Browsing alone does not initialize a reading list. Session cookies may be used to associate a saved list with your browser. Account pages and reading-list responses are marked private and no-store.</p>
+    <p>The hosting infrastructure may process request information to deliver the site. This application does not define the hosting provider's log retention or deletion settings. The <a href={`${import.meta.env.BASE_URL}legal/imprint`}>Imprint</a> explains the site's demo status.</p>
 </LegalLayout>
